the death toll climbed dramatically  overnight after a powerful earthquake  shook iran and iraq more than 340 people  are confirmed dead most of them in Iran  about six thousand others are hurt the  magnitude 7.3 quake struck yesterday  along the border between the two  countries Holly Williams is following  the race to help survivors from Istanbul  Holly good morning good morning there  have so far been more than a hundred  aftershocks since the main earthquake  overnight according to Iranian media the  quake hit during a live TV interview in  Iraq jolting the city of Erbil and  reportedly sending shockwaves all the  way to the shores of the Mediterranean  Sea but the worst damage was around a  hundred and fifty miles to the southeast  across the border in Iran where people's  homes collapsed on top of them a wall  turned over one said this little boy  ever heard it fell on me the quake hit a  poor and mountainous area 70 thousand  people are now reportedly in need of  emergency shelter just as winter closes  in they're still searching for survivors  according to local media the quake  struck along one of many fault lines in  Iran a country where they've grown used  to deadly seismic activity in 2003 an  earthquake near the city of bam killed  around 30,000 people there are also  reports this morning of landslides  caused by the earthquake which could  hamper rescue efforts gale all right  thank you very much Holly Williams
 

